sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Alfred builds Alfred
    accDescr: Kevin asks Alfred for a fix by voice, the engine queues a task, a Claude worker on his laptop builds and tests it on a branch and asks "Ship it?"; a yes is a new task that merges, deploys the engine and publishes a phone release, which the phone verifies and offers to install.
    %% Sources: app/.../service/ClaudeSessionToolbox.kt, server/claude_session/views.py,
    %% tools/claude_session/worker.py, ship.py, build_lock.py, asklist_hook.py,
    %% server/releases/views.py, tools/release_apk.py, app/.../update/UpdateController.kt.
    actor kevin as Kevin
    participant phone as Phone (Alfred)
    participant engine as Engine: /api/claude/tasks
    participant worker as Claude worker (Alienware)
    participant repo as Git: dev and main
    participant cloudrun as Cloud Run
    participant releases as Engine: /api/releases

    kevin->>phone: "fix this" (voice)
    phone->>engine: claude_session tool: new task
    worker->>engine: claim (queued to running)
    worker->>worker: build lock, branch off dev, change, targeted tests
    worker->>engine: finish: needs_confirmation, "Ready: ... Ship it?"
    engine-->>phone: task result
    phone-->>kevin: "Ship it?"
    kevin->>phone: "yes"
    phone->>engine: follow-up task (parent, confirms)
    worker->>engine: claim the yes, one-use ship token
    worker->>repo: rebase, full suites, merge to dev, then main, push
    worker->>cloudrun: deploy the engine, wait, smoke /health
    worker->>releases: assembleFast, release_apk.py publishes the APK
    worker->>engine: finish: done (logged to ships.jsonl)
    phone->>releases: latest release for the phone
    releases-->>phone: signed download link
    phone->>phone: verify sha256 and signer
    phone-->>kevin: "Install the update?"
    kevin->>phone: yes
    phone->>phone: Android installs it
